sec.p:
The description of UCI variable labelled the four saliva measurements as imaginary and real parts with Min(

    Δ

) and Avg(

    Δ

), to suggest sensor-derived change or response variables rather than direct absolute permittivity constants. This distinction was important because the observed values were negative, whereas absolute real permittivity would not normally be interpreted as a negative quantity. Accordingly, Imag_Min, Imag_Avg, Real_Min, and Real_Avg were treated as sensor-derived dielectric response features. They might reflect dielectric changes related to saliva composition, ions, proteins, cells, viscosity, infection, smoking exposure, hydration, or oral conditions, but the public spreadsheet did not allow mechanistic attribution or unit-level physical validation.
